Brings *What the relay stores* in §4.2 in line with `docs/remote-protocol.md` at `82c04e5` (kkrafft1999/snotra#1145, resolving kkrafft1999/snotra#1142):

- the relay-written fields live under `/channels/{channelId}/meta`;
- envelopes are `to-phone|to-desktop/{sid}/{counter}` with `{ c, at }`, no separate nonce (§15);
- the handshake records (§13) and the shapes of the presence records (§12) are listed;
- *Access* says that read access is granted node by node, never on the channel, because the database's rules are not filters;
- *Closed until paired* says the phone reads `meta` and nothing else.

